# Fedora Laptop: UPower battery charge thresholds (ThinkPad E14 Gen 5, BAT0).
#
# Noctalia's Control Center > Power > "Use charge thresholds" toggle calls
# UPower's EnableChargeThreshold over D-Bus. UPower takes its start/stop pair
# from the udev hwdb CHARGE_LIMIT property, not from Noctalia config.
# Without this override the lookup falls through to the vendor default in
# /usr/lib/udev/hwdb.d/60-upower-battery.hwdb (currently also 75,80, but
# owned by the base image and subject to change). Pinning it here keeps
# reinstalls deterministic and documents intent in the repo.
#
# 75,80 = Lenovo conservation behavior: resume charging below 75%, stop at
# 80%. Best for a mostly-docked Li-poly battery; 5% hysteresis avoids
# micro-cycling. For travel days, turn the Noctalia toggle OFF to charge to
# 100%, then turn it back ON when docked again.
# Managed by scripts/configure-system.sh; local edits will conflict.
battery:*:*:dmi:*
 CHARGE_LIMIT=75,80
